@startuml hub-exchange-threats
title One data exchange, and where each threat sits\nthe sign-in, the request through the hub, the DSP negotiation and the DCP credential check, with the STRIDE ids
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
skinparam maxMessageSize 240
skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor #475569
  LifeLineBorderColor #94A3B8
  ParticipantBorderColor #64748B
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  GroupBorderColor #94A3B8
  GroupBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
  DividerBackgroundColor #E2E8F0
}

actor "Person\n(data user)" as P
participant "Keycloak" as KC
box "Hub" #F0F9FF
  participant "UI and API" as UI
  participant "neo4j-proxy" as PX
end box
box "Connectors" #FFFBEB
  participant "Consumer\ncontrol plane" as CCP
  participant "IdentityHub\n+ IssuerService" as IH
  participant "Provider\ncontrol plane" as PCP
  participant "Data plane" as DP
end box
database "Neo4j" as DB

== Sign in and ask ==
P -> KC : sign in (OIDC + PKCE)
note right: S-02 forged session, S-04 realm takeover
KC --> UI : code, then tokens; roles from the realm only
note right: E-03 role injection
P -> UI : request a page or an API route
note right: I-01 anonymous read, E-01 and E-02 wrong role, T-04 CSRF
UI -> UI : requireAuth(): session, roles;\nseesPatientIdentity() by role
UI -> PX : X-Caller (hash of the user), the query
note right: D-01 and D-04 per-user and per-participant rate limit
PX -> DB : parameterised Cypher
note right: T-01 injection, D-03 unbounded query
PX -> DB : audit record, hash-chained
note right: R-01 and R-03 denied access or edited trail
DB --> PX : result, minimum cohort of 5 where federated
note right: I-07 re-identification
PX --> UI : JSON
UI --> P : page

== Negotiate and transfer (DSP 2025-1, DCP v1.0) ==
UI -> CCP : management API, catalog token
note right: I-02 management API exposed, E-04 token misuse
CCP -> PCP : catalog request, contract request
note right: S-01 impersonated participant, T-02 terms changed in transit
PCP -> IH : presentation request (DCP)
IH --> PCP : verifiable presentation: membership, EHDS participant, permit
note right: S-03 replayed presentation, T-03 forged claim,\nI-08 expired or revoked credential accepted
PCP -> PCP : state machine: REQUESTED, AGREED, FINALIZED
note right: T-05 state jump, R-02 denied agreement
PCP --> CCP : contract agreement, signed
CCP -> PCP : transfer request, contractId
PCP -> DP : EDR for this agreement only
note right: E-05 transfer without a contract, D-02 flood
DP --> CCP : FHIR or OMOP data
CCP --> UI : transfer completed
UI -> PX : TransferEvent for the audit trail
PX -> DB : record, hash-chained

legend bottom left
  Each note names the STRIDE ids of the table where that step is analysed. Steps in
  the connectors are the EDC-V implementation's; the project tests them with the
  DSP TCK, the DCP checks and the EHDS suites on every pull request.
endlegend
@enduml
